    "notes": "Modules = py4e.com lessons (install + book chapters 1-16; ch14 OOP is taught after ch13 in Course 4). Coursera mapping recorded as the first entry of each module's topics: C1 Programming for Everybody = install + ch1-5; C2 Python Data Structures = ch6-10; C3 Using Python to Access Web Data = ch11-13; C4 Using Databases with Python = ch14-15; C5 Capstone (Retrieving, Processing, and Visualizing Data with Python) = ch16 visualization worked examples plus peer-graded open-ended projects. The C1-C4 chapter mapping comes from course descriptions via mirror sites (Coursera pages were not fetched directly); Coursera also repeats an install week in later courses. Topics are the html3 book section headings verbatim (Glossary/Exercises omitted), plus 'Lecture:' items taken from py4e.com lesson video titles. Projects = autograder/peer-graded assignments listed on py4e.com lesson pages (quizzes omitted); ch14 lists no autograder; ch16 projects are worked examples rather than graded assignments, and Capstone peer-graded assignment names were not verified. Exercise 7.1 is a worked exercise on the lesson page; only 7.2 is listed as an autograder there (both included). The current online book edition's ch13 has generic 'Application Programming Interfaces' and 'Security and API usage' sections (older editions covered Google geocoding and the Twitter API); the GeoJSON/geocoding API assignment is on py4e.com's own py4e-data proxy. lesson slug 'servces' is a typo on py4e.com, kept as-is in the URL."
